  'hr-policy-update-effective-date-employee-acknowledgment': 'The final check is audience alignment: an acknowledgment counts only against the approved version that the recipient actually received. The report should preserve effective date, language or derivative version, delivery state, and exception owner. This distinguishes a real communication record from a campaign number detached from the governing document. A later owner can then explain why a reminder or correction was necessary. It also keeps a superseded document from being counted as current merely because its campaign remains visible. The record should preserve the correction path and responsible approver for later review.',
  'hr-employee-training-assignment-due-date-integrity': 'The final check is denominator integrity: report the assigned population and course version before interpreting completion. The reviewer should see transfers, exemptions, late assignments, and revised content as explicit movements. That makes a percentage comparable over time without claiming that completion alone proves competence. It also keeps a late or disputed record visible instead of hiding it through a population change. The report should name the observation window and responsible reviewer for every cycle.',
